    <!-- Color Themes definitions -->

    <!-- xbox Colors and Brushes
         xbox themes avoid pure Black and Light due to television specific issues (broadcast safe colors).

         TODO: (http://osgvsowi/8679853)
         1) While there are some websites claiming that all R, G and B should be less than 235 (0xEB) for TVs,
         I did not find any official documents for those broadcast-safe color definitions.
         We will validate following colors with designers when we start working on xbox.

         2) As described previously, we need to use different color schemes for xbox.
         However, the color definitions are mixed up in the following theme dictionaries.
         We would like to seperate WideNarrow and Xbox schemes in the future.
    -->

    <Color x:Key="XboxClrVideoSafeBlackColor">#FF101010</Color>
    <!--R16 G16 B16-->
    <Color x:Key="XboxClrVideoSafeWhiteColor">#FFEBEBEB</Color>
    <!--R235 G235 B235-->

    <!-- CHS Candidate Window Colors and Brushes-->

    <Color x:Key="ChineseHardwareKeyboardBlackColor">#FF2B2B2B</Color>
    <!--R43 G43 B43-->
    <Color x:Key="ChineseHardwareKeyboardGrayColor">#FF767676</Color>
    <!--R118 G118 B118-->
    <Color x:Key="ChineseHardwareKeyboardWhiteColor">#FFF2F2F2</Color>
    <!--R242 G242 B242-->

